1. Nf3 {[%clk 0:15:07.7] lessons from this game:   
- In the classical sicilian after d6, bc4 is the best move.   
- don't be afraid to castle short against the sicilian to turn it into more of a positional battle. Don't castle long just because "it's part of the plan against the sicilian"  
- rather than disregarding my intuition, trust my intuition more - its very strong. Often I'm seeing the best moves as candidates but shrugging them aside and not properly calculating or evaluating the lines. I often pick the "easier" or "safer" moves that aren't as strong.   
- don't move quickly out of frustration, my big mistakes were often made when I thought for only a few seconds} c5 {[%clk 0:15:04.7] } 2. e4 {[%clk 0:15:13.5] } Nc6 {[%clk 0:15:12.4] } 3. d4 {[%clk 0:15:20.3] } cxd4 {[%clk 0:15:20.9] } 4. Nxd4 {[%clk 0:15:27.8] } Nf6 {[%clk 0:15:30] } 5. Nc3 {[%clk 0:15:24.7] going for the classic sicilian - a major weakness of mine in terms of theory} d6 {[%clk 0:15:33.7] }  (5... e6  ) 6. Be2 {[%clk 0:14:50] better was bc4! entering fischer's favourite line}  (6. Bc4! {[%cal Gd1d1,Gc4b3,Ge1c1,Gh1g1,Gg2g4,Gf2f3,Gc1e3,Gd1d2]in the classic sicilian after d6, it's important to recognise that weakens the light squares so bc4 takes advantage of this. white's plan here is not to castle long and create a kingside pawn storm}  ) a6 {[%clk 0:15:31.9] } 7. Be3 {[%clk 0:14:04.5] } e5 {[%clk 0:15:37.6] } 8. Nb3 {[%clk 0:14:04.9] } Be7 {[%clk 0:15:38.4] } 9. f3 {[%clk 0:13:48.7] } O-O {[%clk 0:15:43.7] } 10. Qd2 {[%clk 0:13:54.7] } b5 {[%clk 0:15:51.4] } 11. O-O-O?! {[%clk 0:13:26.8] }  (11. O-O {castling short was better especially after a6 b5, white essentially is saying that it's going to be more of a positional game in nature. Castling long walks right into black's attack which is what he wants. perhaps it was important to recognise that the kingside pawn storm was not quite as strong here because black's attack on the queenside is a bit quicker. castling short makes those moves seem a bit silly and gives me a positional edge on the queenside without having to deal with an attack on my king.}  ) Be6 {[%clk 0:15:58.5] } 12. g4 {[%clk 0:13:13.8] } Nb4 {[%clk 0:16:07.2] } 13. g5 {[%clk 0:11:54.5] }  (13. a3! {I did actually consid4er this and evaluate that the bishop doubling my pawns wasn't the end of the world, I should have gone for this rather than seeing ghosts.}  ) Nd7 {[%clk 0:12:33.5] [%cal Ga2a3]} 14. Nd5 {[%clk 0:11:56.6] perhaps a bit rushed? I just wanted to immediately clarify the tension and get rid of his superficial attack.}  (