g my king to c3 but was worried about c3! doubling my pawns and then rac8 and I can't defend the pawn anymore. I guess that was another reason I played Be1}  (28. b3! {b3 was best immediately getting rid of this clamp which as we saw in the game turned out to be very problematic.}  Rac8 29. Rxc4 Rxc4 30. bxc4 Rxc4 31. Rd3) a5 {[%clk 0:07:37.3] } 29. a4 {[%clk 0:04:54.3] played quickly, out of frastration, but this move is not good, again b3 was best seizing the opportunity to get rid of this c4 clamp}  (29. b3!  ) Nd7 {[%clk 0:07:24.4] } 30. Bf2 {[%clk 0:05:01.7] } Rb8 {[%clk 0:07:04.2] } 31. c3 {[%clk 0:04:06.2] I thought this was necessary to stop c3, crashing through, though positionally I am much worse, with a backwards pawn on b2 the c4 pawn is a very powerful clamp here. My rooks are a bit clumsy and don't have open files either.} Kg7 {[%clk 0:06:09] } 32. Rd2 {[%clk 0:04:08.6] a waiting move, played out of frustration, rg1 was better to hint at ideas of opening up the kingside} f6 {[%clk 0:06:17.5] } 33. gxf6+ {[%clk 0:03:22] } Kxf6 {[%clk 0:06:26.3] I thought nxf6 was much better.}  (33... Nxf6  34. Re1 Nxh5 {I'm a pawn down and in a much worse position}) 34. Bh4+ {[%clk 0:03:13.5] } Kf7 {[%clk 0:05:59.8] } 35. Re1 {[%clk 0:03:10.3] } Nc5 {[%clk 0:06:01.4] } 36. Kc2 {[%clk 0:03:08.8] } Nd3 {[%clk 0:05:50.7] } 37. Rb1 {[%clk 0:03:09.4] } Rb3 {[%clk 0:05:40] }  (37... Rcb7  38. b4 axb4) 38. Rxd3 {[%clk 0:02:59.5] he made a one move blunder and the game is over} Rxb2+ 39. Rxb2 1-0

